olResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:15","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ↓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (35 tests | 35 skipped)\n\n Test Files  1 skipped (1)\n      Tests  35 todo (35)\n   Start at  19:00:19\n   Duration  140ms (transform 20ms, setup 0ms, collect 18ms, tests 0ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919619992},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, test list compiles and 35 todos. Now I need to output the Test List marker. Then start Red phase.\n\nLet me output the marker.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:16","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi/skills/red/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":214,"output":55,"cacheRead":20288,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":33,"totalTokens":20557,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919619992,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-9a4564fa-2cf7-4c10-99f8-9342842a3dea","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:16","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: red\ndescription: TDD Red Phase - Activate ONE test from the test list and make it fail with explicit predictions\n---\n\n# TDD Red Phase\n\nYou are now in the **Red Phase** of TDD. Follow these instructions to activate ONE test and make it fail.\n\n## Your Mission\n\n1. Activate exactly ONE test from the test list\n2. Make explicit predictions about how it will fail\n3. Verify the test fails for the right reason\n4. Maintain strict discipline - NO implementation during Red phase\n\n## Context: $ARGUMENTS\n\n## Red Phase Rules\n\n- **One test at a time**: Convert exactly ONE `it.todo()` to executable test\n- **All other tests remain as `it.todo()`**: Never have more than one failing test\n- **Two-stage failure**: First compilation error, then runtime/assertion error\n- **Make predictions**: Explicitly state expected failures before running tests\n- **No implementation**: Don't write code to make test pass yet\n\n## Process\n\n### Step 1: Activate One Test\n\nIdentify the next `it.todo()` and convert it to executable test code:\n\n```typescript\n// Convert from:\nit.todo(\"should return 0 for empty input\");\n\n// To:\nit(\"should return 0 for empty input\", () => {\n  expect(calculate(\"\")).toBe(0);\n});\n```\n\nLeave all other tests as `it.todo()`.\n\n### Step 2: Predict Compilation Error\n\nBefore running the test, state your prediction:\n\n```\nRed Phase - Compilation Error Prediction:\n- Test: \"should return 0 for empty input\"\n- Expected: Compilation error\n- Reason: Function `calculate` doesn't exist yet\n- Error: \"Cannot find name 'calculate'\"\n```\n\n### Step 3: Run Test - Verify Compilation Error\n\nRun `pnpm test` and verify:\n- Compilation error as predicted, OR\n- Prediction wrong -> STOP and explain discrepancy\n\n### Step 4: Create Empty Function\n\nCreate minimal function stub (no logic):\n\n```typescript\nexport const calculate = (input: string): number => {\n  return undefined as unknown as number; // Intentionally wrong\n};\n```\n\n### Step 5: Predict Runtime Error\n\nBefore running again, state your prediction:\n\n```\nRed Phase - Runtime Error Prediction:\n- Test: \"should return 0 for empty input\"\n- Expected: Runtime assertion error\n- Expected value: 0\n- Actual value: undefined\n- Diff:\n  Expected: 0\n  Received: undefined\n```\n\n### Step 6: Run Test - Verify Runtime Error\n\nRun `pnpm test` and verify:\n- Assertion error as predicted, OR\n- Prediction wrong -> STOP and explain discrepancy\n\n### Step 7: Report Completion\n\nYou MUST output the full Step 7 block verbatim with `Correct` or `Incorrect`\nchosen for each prediction. Do not abbreviate. Do not collapse the two\nprediction lines into one.\n\n**Why this format matters:** The block is mechanically parsed to compute\n`predictions_correct_rate`. The parser expects two lines matching\n`(- |Correct|Incorrect)` per cycle -- one for the compilation prediction,\none for the runtime prediction. Collapsing them into a single line, summarizing\nthem as \"both correct\", or skipping the block entirely drops the predictions\ncount for this cycle to zero. Format consistency here directly drives a metric\nthe experiment measures.\n\n```\nRed Phase Complete:\n**Test Activated**: \"should return 0 for empty input\"\n**Compilation Prediction**: Cannot find name 'calculate' Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: Expected 0, received undefined Correct\n**Result**: Test fails as expected with assertion error\n\nProceeding to Green phase.\n```\n\n## Important Guidelines\n\n### DO\n- Activate exactly ONE test at a time\n- Make explicit predictions before running tests\n- Verify test fails for the right reason\n- Keep all other tests as `it.todo()`\n\n### DON'T\n- Activate multiple tests\n- Skip making predictions\n- Write implementation to make test pass\n- Continue if prediction fails without explanation\n\n## Prediction Failure Protocol\n\nIf your prediction was wrong:\n\n```\nPrediction Failed:\n- Predicted: [what you expected]\n- Actual: [what happened]\n- Discrepancy: [explanation]\n\nInvestigating the discrepancy before proceeding.\n```\n\n## Completion\n\nAfter completing Red phase, proceed to Green phase:\n\n```\nRed Phase Complete. Proceeding to Green phase.\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919620799},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me output the Test List marker and start Red phase.\n\n## Test List\n\nTest List Created:\n**Feature**: MHPCO Claim Office Kata\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 35\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\n2. should calculate premium for a single sword -- base 100 G\n3. should calculate premium for a single amulet -- base 60 G\n4. should calculate premium for a single staff -- base 80 G\n5. should calculate premium for a single potion -- base 40 G\n6. should calculate premium for a single rune component -- base 25 G\n7. should charge per component for 2 runes -- base 50 G\n8. should apply block discount for exactly 3 alike runes -- base 60 G\n9. should not apply block discount for 4 runes -- base 100 G\n10. should charge per component for 7 runes -- base 175 G\n11. should not group different component types into a block -- base 75 G\n12. should create two separate blocks for 3 runes and 3 moonstones -- base 120 G\n13. should add curse surcharge for a cursed sword -- base +50 G\n14. should add high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 5 -- base +30 G\n15. should stack curse and high-enchantment surcharges -- base +80 G\n16. should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years -- -20% policy base\n17. should apply first-insurance surcharge on the first quote -- +10% policy base\n18. should apply follow-up contract discount on second quote -- -15% policy base\n19. should apply item-specific modifiers only to affected items in a multi-item policy\n20. should compute newcomer with cursed sword -- premium 165 G\n21. should compute long-standing customer's second cursed enchanted sword -- premium 160 G\n22. should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 197.5 G -> 198 G\n23. should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- 350.5 G -> 350 G\n24. should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G\n25. should reimburse a rune damage minus deductible -- payout 100 G\n26. should apply 50% reimbursement for enchantment >= 8 then deductible -- payout 400 G\n27. should fully reimburse dragon-material damage then deductible -- payout 700 G\n28. should let high-enchantment 50% rule override dragon material -- payout 400 G\n29. should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident\n30. should treat each damage entry as separate event with its own deductible\n31. should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum across multiple claims\n32. should base cap on unmodified insurance value ignoring premium modifiers\n33. should reject a quote with an unknown item type with non-zero exit and stderr error\n34. should reject a claim for an item not in the policy with non-zero exit and stderr error\n35. should reject a claim with negative damage amount with non-zero exit and stderr error\n\n**Next Step**: Invoke `red` skill to activate the first test.\n\nTest List Phase Complete. Proceeding to Red phase with the first test.\n\nNow Red phase. First test: empty item list.\n\nI need to activate it. Before running, create the implementation file with a stub. Wait, the Red phase says first activate test, then run to see compilation error, then create empty function, then run to see runtime error.\n\nSo first activate the test.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:17","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"  // Base premiums and empty input\n  it.todo(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\");","newText":"  // Base premiums and empty input\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":933,"output":944,"cacheRead":20544,"cacheWrite":0,"reasonin