ductible per damaged item in a single incident\");\n  it.todo(\"should treat each damage entry as separate event with its own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum across multiple claims\");\n  it.todo(\"should base cap on unmodified insurance value ignoring premium modifiers\");\n\n  // Error handling\n  it.todo(\"should reject a quote with an unknown item type with non-zero exit and stderr error\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject a claim for an item not in the policy with non-zero exit and stderr error\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject a claim with negative damage amount with non-zero exit and stderr error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919679740},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (35 tests | 33 skipped) 2ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  2 passed | 33 todo (35)\n   Start at  19:01:19\n   Duration  176ms (transform 25ms, setup 0ms, collect 23ms, tests 2ms, environment 0ms, prepare 50ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919679740},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, tests pass. Now I need to refactor the implementation.\n\n**Step 1: Naming Evaluation**\nCurrent name: `processScenario`\nFunction purpose: Based on the tests, it calculates an insurance premium for a scenario with steps and items.\nQuestion: Does \"processScenario\" clearly reveal intent?\nAssessment: It's somewhat generic. \"processScenario\" could mean many things (process a claim, process a quote, etc.). Based on the tests we have so far, it's specifically computing a premium/quote for given items.\nRecomm