h.ceil, quotePremium = 6 (mass 12)\nConditionals: 0\nLoops: reduce = 1 (mass 5)\nTotal: 31\n\nChanges:\n- Naming: `items` -> `quotedItems` in `quotePremium`; introduced `quoteStep` to clarify use of `scenario.steps[0]`.\n- Structure: removed intermediate `basePremium` variable; `quotePremium` is now an expression body.\n- Kept `basePremiumFor` to preserve the single place that maps item type to base premium (future per-item modifiers).\n\nTests: 7 passing.\n\nDocument decision. Good.\n\nLet's produce final.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring complete.\n\n## Refactoring Report: `src/claim-office.ts`\n\n### Naming Evaluation\n- `processScenario` — still fits; it is the public entry point for a scenario.\n- `quotePremium` — still fits; it calculates the final premium for a quote.\n- `items` parameter in `quotePremium` → renamed to `quotedItems` to clarify that these are the items being quoted.\n- `scenario.steps[0]` → captured as `quoteStep` to reveal that the first step is the quote step.\n\n### Initial APP Mass\n```ts\nconst basePremiumFor = (itemType: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[itemType] ?? 0;\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Array<{ type: string }> | undefined): number => {\n  const basePremium = (items ?? []).reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumFor(item.type), 0);\n  return Math.ceil(basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } => {\n  return { results: [{ premium: quotePremium(scenario.steps[0].items) }] };\n};\n```\n\nComponent count (APP: conditionals counted as `if`/`switch`/`?:` only):\n- Constants: 8 (`5`, `110`, `66`, `88`, `44`, `27.5`, `0`, `0`)\n- Bindings: 6 (`itemType`, `items`, `basePremium`, `sum`, `item`, `scenario`)\n- Invocations: 6 (`reduce`, `+`, `basePremiumFor`, `+`, `Math.ceil`, `quotePremium`) → mass 12\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Loops: 1 (`reduce`) → mass 5\n\n**Total Mass: 31**\n\n### Refactored APP Mass\n```ts