king":"Tests pass. Green marker.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Green -- Added high-enchantment surcharge for level >= 5\n\nGreen Phase Complete:\n**Implementation**: Added HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD/RATE and condition in itemModifierAmount\n**Result**: All tests now pass (14 passing)\n**Approach**: Minimal addition to item modifier logic\n\nProceeding to Refactor phase."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.subagent:115","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 14\nRecent changes: Added high-enchantment surcharge for level >= 5\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":254,"output":166,"cacheRead":77120,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":77540,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920310339,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0bdaaca2-74b7-463e-88eb-26a910df931e","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:115","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Summary\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- `processScenario`: Name kept. It processes an MHPCO scenario (currently the quote step; claim steps will follow). The name still fits.\n- `calculateQuotePremium`: The \"calculate\" prefix is redundant for a function that returns a premium. Renamed to `quotePremium`.\n- `policyBasePremium`: It computes the base premium derived from items only, before policy-wide modifiers. Renamed to `itemsBasePremium` for accuracy.\n- `itemModifierAmount`: After adding the high-enchantment surcharge, this function sums item-specific surcharges. Renamed to `itemSurchargeAmount` to reveal that intent.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (`itemModifierAmount`):\n\n```typescript\nconst itemModifierAmount = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumFor(item.type);\n  let modifier = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) {\n    modifier += base * CURSE_RATE;\n  }\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    modifier += base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return modifier;\n};\n```\n\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 2 (literal `0`s) = 2\n- Bindings: 5 (item, base, modifier, CURSE_RATE, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) = 5\n- Invocations: 5 (basePremiumFor, `*`, `*`, `??`, `>=`) = 10\n- Conditionals: 2 (if statements) = 8\n- Loops: 0 = 0\n- Assignments: 3 (let modifier = 0, +=, +=) = 18\n\nTotal Mass: 43\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (`itemSurchargeAmount`):\n\n```typescript\nconst itemSurchargeAmount = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumFor(item.type);\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge = (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n```\n\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 2 (literal `0`s) = 2\n- Bindings: 6 (item, base, CURSE_RATE, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD, curseSurcharge, enchantmentSurcharge) = 6\n- Invocations: 6 (basePremiumFor, `*`, `*`, `??`, `>=`, `+`) = 12\n- Conditionals: 2 (ternaries) = 8\n- Loops: 0 = 0\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n\nTotal Mass: 28  \nMass Change: 43 → 28 (delta -15, ~35% reduction)\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Naming: Renamed `calculateQuotePremium` → `quotePremium`, `policyBasePremium` → `itemsBasePremium`, and `itemModifierAmount` → `itemSurchargeAmount`.\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent): Replaced mutable `modifier` accumulation with explaining variables `curseSurcharge` and `enchantmentSurcharge`, making each surcharge explicit.\n- Rule 3/APP: Removed mutable assignments, lowering mass.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): No new abstractions introduced; changes are minimal.\n\nBenefits:\n- Function names now describe what they return/compute.\n- Each surcharge is computed declaratively, improving readability.\n- Mass reduced by eliminating mutable state in the primary refactored function.\n\n**Refactoring Complete**:\n- Refactoring: Renamed functions for clarity and refactored item surcharge calculation to use explaining variables.\n- Mass Change: 43 → 28 for `itemSurchargeAmount`.\n- Tests: All 14 passing tests remain green."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 14\nRecent changes: Added high-enchantment surcharge for level >= 5\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 14\nRecent changes: Added high-enchantment surcharge for level >= 5\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784920312728},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by examining the project structure and the relevant files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:2","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi/agents/refactor/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":82,"output":72,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":14,"totalTokens":5722,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920312748,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-08ff1be2-5be6-4c5c-9dd3-43d908baaa74","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Base premiums and empty input\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single sword -- final premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single amulet -- final premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single staff -- final premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 93 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single potion -- final premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 49 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single rune component -- final premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Component building blocks\n  it(\"should charge per component for 2 runes -- final premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply block discount for exactly 3 alike runes -- final premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should not apply block discount for 4 runes -- final premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should charge per component for 7 runes -- final premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Alike components\n  it(\"should not group different component types into a block -- final premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 88 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should create two separate blocks for 3 runes and 3 moonstones -- final premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n        { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 137 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should add curse surcharge for a cursed sword -- final premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 5 -- final premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }] });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should stack curse and high-enchantment surcharges -- base +80 G\");\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years -- -20% policy base\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply first-insurance surcharge on the first quote -- +10% policy base\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on second quote -- -15% policy base\");\n\n  // Multi-item and integration\n  it.todo(\"should apply item-specific modifiers only to affected items in a multi-item policy\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute newcomer with cursed sword -- premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute long-standing customer's second cursed enchanted sword -- premium 160 G\");\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 197.5 G -> 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- 350.5 G -> 350 G\");\n\n  // Claim processing - basic reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse a rune damage minus deductible -- payout 100 G\");\n\n  // Claim processing - special clauses\n  it.todo(\"should apply 50% reimbursement for enchantment >= 8 then deductible -- payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage then deductible -- payout 700 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should let high-enchantment 50% rule override dragon material -- payout 400 G\");\n\n  // Claim processing - multiple damages and caps\n  it.todo(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident\");\n  it.todo(\"should treat each damage entry as separate event with its own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum across multiple claims\");\n  it.todo(\"should base cap on unmodified insurance value ignoring premium modifiers\");\n\n  // Error handling\n  it.todo(\"should reject a quote with an unknown item type with non-zero exit and stderr error\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject a claim for an item not in the policy with non-zero exit and stderr error\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject a claim with negative damage amount with non-zero exit and stderr error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920313961},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.3;\n\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number };\n\ntype Scenario = {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Array<{ op: string; items?: Item[] }>;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (itemType: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[itemType] ?? 0;\n\nconst premiumForComponentGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES.includes(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PRICE;\n  }\n  return count * basePremiumFor(type);\n};\n\nconst policyBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const groups = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    groups.set(item.type, (groups.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of groups) {\n    total += premiumForComponentGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst itemModifierAmount = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumFor(item.type);\n  let modifier = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) {\n    modifier += base * CURSE_RATE;\n  }\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    modifier += base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return modifier;\n};\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (items: Item[] | undefined = []): number => {\n  const policyBase = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const itemModifiers = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemModifierAmount(item), 0);\n  const firstInsurance = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n  return Math.ceil(policyBase + itemModifiers + firstInsurance + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } => {\n  const quoteStep = scenario.steps[0];\n  return { results: [{ premium: calculateQuotePremium(quoteStep.items) }] };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920313961},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents/refactor/SKILL.md'"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784920313961},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me find the refactor skill/agent file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.find:3","name":"find","arguments":{"pattern":".pi/**/refactor*"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.find:4","name":"find","arguments":{"pattern":"**/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":2534,"output":47,"cacheRead":5696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":10,"totalTokens":8277,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920313962,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-2529a942-9473-4d9e-bb9c-9eda8d3b2014","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.find:3","toolName":"find","content":[{"type":"text","text":".pi/agents/refactor.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920314738},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.find:4","toolName":"find","content":[{"type":"text","text":".pi/skills/green/SKILL.md\n.pi/skills/red/SKILL.md\n.pi/skills/test-list/SKILL.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920314738},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me read the refactor agent instructions.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:5","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi/agents/refactor.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":80,"output":30,"cacheRead":8256,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":9,"totalTokens":8366,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920314738,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-06138501-d28c-4504-9a42-d659c7b1d7a2","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:5","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: refactor\ndescription: Refactoring specialist. Applies Simple Design Rules and the Absolute Priority Premise (APP) to improve code while keeping all tests green. Returns a summary of what changed and why.\ntools: read, write, edit, bash, grep, find, ls\n---\n\n\n## Your Mission\n\nGuide the requester through a refactoring pass by helping them:\n1. **MUST attempt at least one refactoring** - mandatory, not optional\n2. Apply the Four Rules of Simple Design in priority order\n3. Use Absolute Priority Premise (APP) to measure code improvements\n4. Improve code quality while keeping all tests green\n5. Document refactoring decisions and mass calculations\n6. If no improvement is possible, explicitly document why\n\n## Refactoring Rules\n\n- **Mandatory refactoring attempt**: MUST try at least one improvement\n- **Tests must stay green**: Never break passing tests\n- **Apply Simple Design Rules**: In priority order (1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4)\n- **Calculate APP mass**: Before and after refactoring\n- **Document decisions**: Explain improvements or why none were possible\n- **Naming is first priority**: Evaluate if function name still fits its purpose\n\n### Simple Design Rules (Priority Order)\n\n#### Rule 1: Tests Pass\n- **Highest priority** - never compromise working code\n- All tests must pass before and after refactoring\n- If tests fail, revert and try different approach\n\n#### Rule 2: Reveals Intent\n- **Second priority** - clarity trumps everything else (including APP)\n- Use meaningful names for variables, functions, classes\n- Structure code to be self-documenting\n- Prefer explicit over clever code\n- **Naming Evaluation (First Refactoring Priority)**:\n  - Ask: \"Does this name clearly describe what the function actually does based on all tests we have so far?\"\n  - Ask: \"Has the function's purpose become clearer/more specific through the latest test?\"\n  - Rename if the name doesn't capture the current full intent\n  - Especially critical when new functionality changes the nature of what the function does\n\n#### Rule 3: No Duplication (DRY)\n- **Third priority** - extract common functionality\n- Look for obvious and conceptual duplication\n- Knowledge should have single representation\n- **Balance with Rule 2**: If DRY hurts clarity, choose clarity\n\n#### Rule 4: Fewest Elements\n- **Lowest priority** - minimize code elements\n- Remove unnecessary abstractions\n- Keep it simple - don't over-engineer\n- Only add complexity when it serves clear purpose\n\n### Absolute Priority Premise (APP)\n\n#### Mass Calculation\n```\nTotal Mass = (constants x 1) + (bindings x 1) + (invocations x 2) +\n             (conditionals x 4) + (loops x 5) + (assignments x 6)\n```\n\n#### Component Values\n- **Constant** (Mass: 1): Literal values (`5`, `\"hello\"`, `true`)\n- **Binding/Scalar** (Mass: 1): Variables, parameters (`amount`, `result`)\n- **Invocation** (Mass: 2): Function calls (`calculate()`, `Math.max()`)\n- **Conditional** (Mass: 4): Control flow (`if`, `switch`, `?:`)\n- **Loop** (Mass: 5): Iteration (`for`, `forEach`, `map`)\n- **Assignment** (Mass: 6): Mutations (`x = 5`, `count++`)\n\n#### Guidelines\n- **Lower mass = Better code** (generally)\n- **Rule 2 trumps APP**: Clarity over low mass\n- **Use during refactoring**: Compare before/after mass\n- **Context matters**: Don't sacrifice readability for mass\n\n## Refactoring Process\n\n### Step 1: Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY)\nBefore anything else, evaluate the naming:\n```\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current name: `calculate`\n- Function purpose: \"adds numbers from an array\"\n- Question: Does \"calculate\" clearly reveal this intent?\n- Assessment: Too generic - \"calculate\" could mean anything\n- Recommendation: Rename to `sumNumbers` or keep if name fits\n\nDecision: [Rename to X] or [Keep current name because Y]\n```\n\n### Step 2: Calculate Initial APP Mass\nBefore making changes, calculate current code mass:\n```\n**Current Code Mass**:\nfunction calculate(numbers: number[]): number {\n  return numbers.reduce((sum, num) => sum + num, 0);\n}\n\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 1 (literal 0) = 1\n- Bindings: 3 (numbers, sum, num) = 3\n- Invocations: 2 (reduce, +) = 4\n- Conditionals: 0 = 0\n- Loops: 1 (reduce is iteration) = 5\n- Assignments: 0 = 0\n\nTotal Mass: 13\n```\n\n### Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules (in order)\nSystematically evaluate each rule:\n\n#### Evaluate Rule 1: Tests Pass\n- Are all tests currently passing?\n- If not, fix before refactoring\n\n#### Evaluate Rule 2: Reveals Intent\n- Are names clear and descriptive?\n- Is code structure self-documenting?\n- Can intent be improved?\n\nPotential improvements:\n- Rename variables for clarity\n- Extract explaining variables\n- Rename functions to match purpose\n- Restructure for readability\n\n#### Evaluate Rule 3: No Duplication\n- Is there duplicated code?\n- Is there conceptual duplication?\n- Can common logic be extracted?\n\nPotential improvements:\n- Extract helper functions\n- Remove copy-paste code\n- Consolidate similar logic\n\n#### Evaluate Rule 4: Fewest Elements\n- Are there unnecessary abstractions?\n- Can code be simplified?\n- Are all elements necessary?\n\nPotential improvements:\n- Remove unused functions/variables\n- Simplify over-engineered solutions\n- Inline unnecessary extractions\n\n### Step 4: Implement Refactoring\n- Make ONE improvement at a time\n- Run tests after each change\n- Ensure tests stay green\n- If tests fail, revert change\n\n### Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\nAfter refactoring, recalculate mass:\n```\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n[refactored code]\n\nComponent Count:\n[detailed breakdown]\n\nTotal Mass: [new total]\nMass Change: [old mass] -> [new mass] (delta [difference])\n```\n\n### Step 6: Document Decision\nExplain the refactoring outcome:\n\n**If Improvements Made:**\n```\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Naming: Renamed `calculate` to `sumNumbers` (better reveals intent)\n- Mass: Reduced from 13 to 11 (removed conditional)\n- Rule 2: Improved clarity with explaining variable\n\nBenefits:\n- Code now clearly states it sums numbers\n- Reduced complexity (lower mass)\n- More maintainable\n```\n\n**If No Improvements Possible:**\n```\n**Refactoring Evaluation**:\n- Naming: `calculate` already clearly describes purpose\n- Duplication: No duplicated code found\n- Mass: Current implementation already minimal (mass: 13)\n- Simplification: No unnecessary complexity\n\nReasoning:\nCurrent implementation is already optimal because:\n1. Name clearly reveals intent\n2. No duplication exists\n3. Mass is minimal for this functionality\n4. No unnecessary abstractions\n\nNo refactoring performed - code is already clean.\n```\n\n### Step 7: Report Completion\n```\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: [improvements made or \"none possible\"]\n**Mass Change**: [before -> after] (if calculated)\n**Tests**: All passing\n```\n\nReturn the report to the requester.\n\n## Important Guidelines\n\n### What to DO\n- MUST attempt at least one refactoring\n- Evaluate naming FIRST\n- Calculate APP mass before and after\n- Apply Simple Design Rules in priority order\n- Keep tests green at all times\n- Document all decisions\n- Explain why if no improvement possible\n\n### What NOT to do\n- Never return without attempting at least one improvement\n- Never break tests during refactoring\n- Never sacrifice clarity for lower mass\n- Never refactor multiple things at once\n- Never say \"no refactoring needed\" without detailed explanation\n\n## Remember\n\n- **Mandatory refactoring attempt** - MUST try at least one improvement\n- **Naming first** - Always evaluate function names first\n- **Tests stay green** - Never break passing tests\n- **Simple Design Rules** - Apply in priority order (1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4)\n- **Rule 2 trumps APP** - Clarity over low mass\n- **Document everything** - Mass calculations and decisions\n\nYour goal is to systematically improve code quality using established principles, measure improvements objectively with APP, and maintain transparency through comprehensive documentation.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920315341},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the refactor instructions. Let me first run the tests to confirm they pass. Then evaluate naming and mass.\n\nI need to:\n1. Run tests to confirm green\n2. Evaluate naming\n3. Calculate APP mass\n4. Find at least one refactoring\n5. Apply it\n6. Recalculate mass\n7. Document\n\nLet me first run tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:6","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1876,"output":101,"cacheRead":8320,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":77,"totalTokens":10297,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920315342,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-edf756f9-9a9f-4ffb-bb06-e4b7d586eb5e","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:6","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (35 tests | 21 skipped) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  14 passed | 21 todo (35)\n   Start at  19:11:56\n   Duration  154ms (transform 28ms, setup 0ms, collect 27ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920316820},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Tests pass. Now let me evaluate naming.\n\nNames in the code:\n- `processScenario` - This processes an MHPCO scenario. Seems OK.\n- `calculateQuotePremium` - Calculates premium for a quote. OK.\n- `policyBasePremium` - Calculates base premium for items. OK.\n- `premiumForComponentGroup` - Calculates premium for a group of components. OK.\n- `itemModifierAmount` - Calculates item-specific modifier amount. OK.\n- `basePremiumFor` - Gets base premium for item type. OK.\n- Constants are OK.\n\nPotential improvements:\n1. `itemModifierAmount` - The function name says it returns an amount, which is fine. But it could be more explicit: `itemSurchargeAmount` or `itemSpecificModifier`. Actually `itemModifierAmount` is clear enough.\n2. `policyBasePremium` - returns the base premium of the items before modifiers and surcharges. But \"policyBasePremium\" could be confused. The tests show it's the sum of base item premiums with component block discounts. Maybe `itemsBasePremium` or `componentBasePremium` would be clearer.\n3. `calculateQuotePremium` - It's a function that calculates quote premium. Could be just `quotePremium`.\n4. `processScenario` - Currently only handles quote step. Maybe `processQuote`? But tests mention claim processing too, so the scenario will have multiple steps. The function name `processScenario` is fine.\n\nLooking at potential duplication:\n- In `policyBasePremium`, it iterates items and groups by type. In `calculateQuotePremium`, it uses `items.reduce()` for modifiers. Different purposes.\n- `basePremiumFor` is used twice.\n\nPotential issues:\n- `COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES` is only used in `premiumForComponentGroup`. Could inline but that doesn't help much.\n- `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE` is always applied to `policyBase` in `calculateQuotePremium`, even though tests only have first quote. Tests haven't added first-insurance test yet but the code applies it unconditionally. This is probably intentional based on the recent green