hantment 8.\n\nActually, the policy stores item details. The damage entry only has itemType and amount. The item's enchantment and material come from the policy. So the policy's sword has enchantment 8.\n\nSo test 23 scenario:\n- steps[0]: quote with sword enchantment 8.\n- steps[1]: claim policy 0 with damage sword amount 901.\nExpected: results [{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 350, remainingCap: 1850 }] (cap = 2 * 1000 = 2000, payout 350, remaining 1650? Wait, 2000 - 350 = 1650).\n\nWait, payout 350.5 rounded down to 350. Remaining cap = 2000 - 350 = 1650.\n\nBut for the rounding test, I only need to verify payout is 350. The remainingCap can be checked too.\n\nThis test requires full claim processing. I'll implement minimal claim processing: process each damage, apply clauses, deductible, cap.\n\nBut that's a lot. Let me start with test 24 (basic claim) instead? No, I need to follow order. But test 23 will require the same infrastructure. Let me implement it.\n\nActually, maybe I should activate tests 24 and 25 first since they're simpler and build up claim processing. But the instructions say follow the test list. However, if I implement claim processing for test 23, tests 24-25 will pass too.\n\nLet me activate test 23 and implement claim processing.\n\nFirst, I'll need to store policies. For each quote step, store the items and insurance sum. For claim step, look up policy by index, process damages.\n\nInsurance values:\n- sword: 1000\n- amulet: 600\n- staff: 800\n- potion: 400\n- rune/moonstone: 250 each\n\nCap = 2 * sum of insurance values.\n\nFor each damage entry:\n- Find item in policy with matching type. If multiple items of same type, we need to track which one? The spec says each damage entry is a separate damage event. For type matching, if there are multiple items of same type, we just need at least one. But the spec also says if damages has more entries of a type than policy covers, reject. For now, minimal: check count.\n\nFor payout per damage:\n- If dragon material: full reimbursement.\n- Else if enchantment >= 8: 50% of damage.\n- Else: full reimbursement.\n- Then deductible 100.\n\nSum all damage payouts. Then apply cap: min(sum, remainingCap). Update remainingCap.\n\nRounding: final payout rounded down (MHPCO's favor).\n\nThis is complex. Let me implement minimally.\n\nActually, the green phase says minimal. But implementing all claim logic at once is needed. I'll do it in one go.\n\nLet me update the implementation.</think>"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:146","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"  it.todo(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- 350.5 G -> 350 G\");","newText":"  it(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- 350.5 G -> 350 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 8 }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 901 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 350, remainingCap: 1650 }] });\n  });"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":228,"output":1571,"cacheRead":93696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":6,"totalTokens":95495,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920594545,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-2ace0812-05ce-42d4-bea3-45b54fccaa09","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:146","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim-office.spec.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 180       steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }],\n 181     });\n 182     expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n 183  