area (`policyCapFor` + `POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER` + usage): 3 → 7\n- Total changed: 75 → 69 (-6)\n\nI think this is clear.\n\nLet me finalize the report.\n\nOne more thing: I should mention that tests stayed green after each refactoring step. That's part of the process.\n\nOK, writing the final response now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Report\n\n### Naming Evaluation\n\n| Current Name | Purpose | Assessment | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `rateAmountIf` | Returns `base * rate` when a condition applies, otherwise `0` | Name is terse and the `If` suffix reads as a side-effect; intent is clearer with a noun phrase | **Rename to `conditionalRateAmount`** |\n| `damagePayout` | Computes reimbursement for one damage entry, applying special item clauses and deductible | Name is fine, but the implementation hides the dragon-material rule behind a redundant assignment, making the precedence unclear | Keep name, refactor internals |\n| `policyInsuranceSum(items) * 2` | Cap for a policy is twice the insurance sum | Magic `2` and inline math hide the business rule | **Extract `policyCapFor` + `POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER`** |\n| Inline return expression in `quotePremium` | Sum of base, surcharges, discounts, and fee | Very long line obscures the arithmetic | **Extract `subtotal`** |\n\n### Initial APP Mass\n\nMeasured on the functions/areas changed:\n\n```text\nrateAmountIf                : 8\nquotePremium                : 28\ndamagePayout                : 36\nprocessScenario cap snippet : 3\n----------------------------------\nTotal                       : 75\n```\n\nComponent counts:\n\n- `rateAmountIf`: 1 constant + 3 bindings + 1 conditional = 8\n- `quotePremium`: 1 constant + 10 bindings + 6 invocations + 1 loop = 28\n- `damagePayout`: 5 constants + 3 bindings + 1 invocation + 2 conditionals + 3 assignments = 36\n\n### Refactorings Applied\n\n1. **Naming** — Renamed `rateAmountIf` → `conditionalRateAmount`.\n2. **Clarity / DRY** — Replaced magic numbers in damage logic with named constants:\n   - `DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100`\n   - `DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8`\n   - `DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.5`\n3. **Clarity** — Extracted `damageReimbursementRate(item)` to make dragon-material (100 %) and high-enchantment (50 %) rules explicit, eliminating the confusing redundant dragon branch and the mutable `let reimbursement`.\n4. **Clarity** — Extracted a `subtotal` variable in `quotePremium` so the premium arithmetic is readable.\n5. **Clarity** — Extracted `policyCapFor(items)` and `POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER` to name the \"cap is twice the insurance sum\" rule.\n\nEach change was followed by `pnpm test`; all 23 passing tests remained green.\n\n### New APP Mass\n\n```text\nconditionalRateAmount                    : 8\nquotePremium                             : 29\ndamagePayout + damageReimbursementRate   : 25\npolicyCapFor + POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER     : 7\n-------------------------------------------\nTotal                                    : 69\n```\n\nMass change: **75 → 69 (−6)**.\n\n### Rule-by-Rule Assessment\n\n- **Rule 1 — Tests Pass**: ✅ All 23 tests green after every step.\n- **Rule 2 — Reveals Intent**: ✅ `conditionalRateAmount`, `damageReimbursementRate`, `policyCapFor`, and `subtotal` all make the business rules explicit.\n- **Rule 3 — No Duplication**: ✅ Magic numbers removed; damage-rate logic has a single representation.\n- **Rule 4 — Fewest Elements**: ✅ Added small, focused helpers only where they improve clarity; no unnecessary abstractions.\n\n### Trade-offs\n\n- `quotePremium` mass increased by 1 (new `subtotal` binding) — accepted per Rule 2 (clarity over lower mass).\n- `policyCapFor` area mass increased by 4 — accepted because it names a business rule that was previously a bare `* 2`.\n\n### Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `rateAmountIf`, extracted `conditionalRateAmount`; extracted `damageReimbursementRate` and damage constants; extracted `subtotal` in `quotePremium`; extracted `policyCapFor` and `POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER`.\n\n**Mass Change**: 75 → 69 (−6)\n\n**Tests**: All passing — 23 passed, 12 todo."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":160,"output":1486,"cacheRead":30528,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":574,"totalTokens":32174,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784920695687,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-37a4b7bb-f666-4203-8aff-4dd2a289f16d","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":9066,"output":17939,"cacheRead":316480,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":32174,"turns":16},"model":"requesty/tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920701625},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Verify.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:152","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test 2>&1 | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":931,"output":29,"cacheRead":98176,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3,"totalTokens":99136,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920701633,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-af23d2ff-fcd6-4207-81a5-81403c9f72ae","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:152","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (35 tests | 12 skipped) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  23 passed | 12 todo (35)\n   Start at  19:18:23\n   Duration  172ms (transform 33ms, setup 0ms, collect 31ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 49ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920703966},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Read current file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:153","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":285,"output":25,"cacheRead":99072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5,"totalTokens":99382,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920703969,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-490c3796-917b-492c-92c9-81a69cb383ad","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:153","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const conditionalRateAmount = (\n  applies: boolean,\n  base: number,\n  rate: number,\n): number => (applies ? base * rate : 0);\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst LOYALTY_RATE = 0.2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst CURSE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.3;\n\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number; material?: string };\n\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items?: Item[] };\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: { cause: string; damages: Damage[] } };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ntype Scenario = {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (itemType: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[itemType] ?? 0;\nconst insuranceValueFor = (itemType: string): number => INSURANCE_VALUES[itemType] ?? 0;\n\nconst countItemsByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst premiumForComponentGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES.includes(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PRICE;\n  }\n  return count * basePremiumFor(type);\n};\n\nconst itemsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of countItemsByType(items)) {\n    total += premiumForComponentGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst itemSurchargeAmount = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumFor(item.type);\n  const curseSurcharge = conditionalRateAmount(item.cursed ?? false, base, CURSE_RATE);\n  const enchantmentSurcharge = conditionalRateAmount(\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n    base,\n    HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE,\n  );\n  return curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst quotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number },\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  const itemsBase = itemsBasePremium(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemSurchargeAmount(item), 0);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = itemsBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount = conditionalRateAmount(\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD,\n    itemsBase,\n    LOYALTY_RATE,\n  );\n  const followUpDiscount = conditionalRateAmount(\n    quoteIndex > 0,\n    itemsBase,\n    FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_RATE,\n  );\n  const subtotal =\n    itemsBase +\n    itemSurcharges +\n    firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n    loyaltyDiscount -\n    followUpDiscount +\n    PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return Math.ceil(subtotal);\n};\n\ntype Policy = { items: Item[]; cap: number };\n\nconst policyInsuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueFor(item.type), 0);\n\nconst policyCapFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  policyInsuranceSum(items) * POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst damageReimbursementRate = (item: Item): number => {\n  if (item.material === \"dragon\") return 1;\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) return DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE;\n  return 1;\n};\n\nconst damagePayout = (damage: Damage, item: Item): number => {\n  const reimbursement = damage.amount * damageReimbursementRate(item);\n  return Math.max(0, reimbursement - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst claimResult = (policy: Policy, incident: ClaimStep[\"incident\"]): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  let payout = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!item) {\n      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} is not part of the policy`);\n    }\n    payout += damagePayout(damage, item);\n  }\n  const cappedPayout = Math.min(payout, policy.cap);\n  const roundedPayout = Math.floor(cappedPayout);\n  return { payout: roundedPayout, remainingCap: policy.cap - roundedPayout };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): { results: Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> } => {\n  const results: Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> = [];\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  let quoteIndex = 0;\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      policies.push({ items, cap: policyCapFor(items) });\n      results.push({ premium: quotePremium(items, scenario.customer, quoteIndex) });\n      quoteIndex++;\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policy = policies[step.policy];\n      const result = claimResult(policy, step.incident);\n      policy.cap = result.remainingCap;\n      results.push(result);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920706095},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now Red for test 24: standard reimbursement regular steel sword damage 500 → payout 400.\n\nThis should pass with current claim logic. Let me activate.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:154","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"  it.todo(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G\");","newText":"  it(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }] });\n  });"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1533,"output":253,"cacheRead":99328,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":33,"totalTokens":101114,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920706100,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-5f06bb67-6f62-4da9-a3ce-7a0adaf3df37","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functi