"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":275,"output":173,"cacheRead":106112,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7,"totalTokens":106560,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920741338,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d72e12f5-a020-41ef-9cc5-8261ac4213d9","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:167","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring Applied**: Simplified `damageReimbursementRate` by removing the redundant dragon-material branch and collapsing the two identical `return 1` paths into a single ternary expression. High-enchantment still takes precedence as required by the recent change; dragon material and all other cases fall through to the default full reimbursement rate (`1`).\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- `damageReimbursementRate`: name clearly describes that it returns the reimbursement rate for a damage claim. Kept.\n- The dragon-material clause no longer needs its own branch because the default return already expresses \"full reimbursement,\" eliminating conceptual duplication without harming intent.\n\n**APP Mass Calculation**:\n\nBefore:\n```typescript\nconst damageReimbursementRate = (item: Item): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) return DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE;\n  if (item.material === \"dragon\") return 1;\n  return 1;\n};\n```\n- Constants: `0`, `DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD`, `DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE`, `\"dragon\"`, `1`, `1` → 6\n- Bindings: `item` → 1\n- Invocations: `??`, `>=`, `===` → 6\n- Conditionals: `if`, `if` → 8\n- **Total Mass: 21**\n\nAfter:\n```typescript\nconst damageReimbursementRate = (item: Item): number =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD ? DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE : 1;\n```\n- Constants: `0`, `DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD`, `DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE`, `1` → 4\n- Bindings: `item` → 1\n- Invocations: `??`, `>=` → 4\n- Conditionals: `?:` → 4\n- **Total Mass: 13**\n\n**Mass Change**: 21 → 13 (delta −8)\n\n**Simple Design Rules Applied**:\n1. **Tests Pass**: all 28 passing tests remain green.\n2. **Reveals Intent**: the ternary directly expresses \"high enchantment reduces reimbursement; otherwise full rate.\"\n3. **No Duplication**: removed the duplicated `return 1` for dragon/default material cases.\n4. **Fewest Elements**: removed an unnecessary conditional branch and constant reference.\n\n**Tests**: All 28 passing, 7 todo."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 28\nRecent changes: Swapped damage clause precedence so high enchantment overrides dragon material\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 28\nRecent changes: Swapped damage clause precedence so high enchantment overrides dragon material\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784920743901},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by understanding the task. I need to refactor the implementation in `src/claim-office.ts` while keeping all tests green. The recent change was swapping damage clause precedence so high enchantment overrides dragon material.\n\nFirst, I should read the implementation file and test file to understand the current state.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":83,"output":100,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":62,"totalTokens":5751,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784920743920,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-a77010f6-2645-41fb-8f30-e3951900be1f","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const conditionalRateAmount = (\n  applies: boolean,\n  base: number,\n  rate: number,\n): number => (applies ? base * rate : 0);\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst LOYALTY_RATE = 0.2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst CURSE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.3;\n\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number; material?: string };\n\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items?: Item[] };\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: { cause: string; damages: Damage[] } };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ntype Scenario = {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (itemType: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[itemType] ?? 0;\nconst insuranceValueFor = (itemType: string): number => INSURANCE_VALUES[itemType] ?? 0;\n\nconst countItemsByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst premiumForComponentGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES.includes(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PRICE;\n  }\n  return count * basePremiumFor(type);\n};\n\nconst itemsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of countItemsByType(items)) {\n    total += premiumForComponentGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst itemSurchargeAmount = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumFor(item.type);\n  const curseSurcharge = conditionalRateAmount(item.cursed ?? false, base, CURSE_RATE);\n  const enchantmentSurcharge = conditionalRateAmount(\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n    base,\n    HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE,\n  );\n  return curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst quotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number },\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): number => {\n  const itemsBase = itemsBasePremium(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemSurchargeAmount(item), 0);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = itemsBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount = conditionalRateAmount(\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD,\n    itemsBase,\n    LOYALTY_RATE,\n  );\n  const followUpDiscount = conditionalRateAmount(\n    quoteIndex > 0,\n    itemsBase,\n    FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_RATE,\n  );\n  const subtotal =\n    itemsBase +\n    itemSurcharges +\n    firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n    loyaltyDiscount -\n    followUpDiscount +\n    PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return Math.ceil(subtotal);\n};\n\ntype Policy = { items: Item[]; cap: number };\n\nconst policyInsuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueFor(item.type), 0);\n\nconst policyCapFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  policyInsuranceSum(items) * POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst damageReimbursementRate = (item: Item): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) return DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE;\n  if (item.material === \"dragon\") return 1;\n  return 1;\n};\n\nconst damagePayout = (damage: Damage, item: Item): number => {\n  const reimbursement = damage.amount * damageReimbursementRate(item);\n  return Math.max(0, reimbursement - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst claimResult = (policy: Policy, incident: ClaimStep[\"incident\"]): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  let payout = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!item) {\n      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} is not part of the policy`);\n    }\n    payout += damagePayout(damage, item);\n  }\n  const cappedPayout = Math.min(payout, policy.cap);\n  const roundedPayout = Math.floor(cappedPayout);\n  return { payout: roundedPayout, remainingCap: policy.cap - roundedPayout };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): { results: Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> } => {\n  const results: Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> = [];\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  let quoteIndex = 0;\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      policies.push({ items, cap: policyCapFor(items) });\n      results.push({ premium: quotePremium(items, scenario.customer, quoteIndex) });\n      quoteIndex++;\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policy = policies[step.policy];\n      const result = claimResult(policy, step.incident);\n      policy.cap = result.remainingCap;\n      results.push(result);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784920744819},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Base premiums and empty input\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single sword -- final premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single amulet -- final premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single staff -- final premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 93 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single potion -- final premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 49 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single rune component -- final premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Component building blocks\n  it(\"should charge per component for 2 runes -- final premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply block discount for exactly 3 alike runes -- final premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should not apply block discount for 4 runes -- final premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should charge per component for 7 runes -- final premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Alike components\n  it(\"should not group different component types into a block -- final premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 88 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should create two separate blocks for 3 runes and 3 moonstones -- final premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n        { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 137 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should add curse surcharge for a cursed sword -- final premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 5 -- final premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should stack curse and high-enchantment surcharges -- final premium 195 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 195 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it(\"should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years -- final premium 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 95 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply first-insurance surcharge on the first quote -- final premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on second quote -- final premiums 115 G and 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }, { premium: 100 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Multi-item and integration\n  it(\"should apply item-specific modifiers only to affected items in a multi-item policy -- final premium 231 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n        { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n        { type: \"amulet\" },\n      ] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 231 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute newcomer with cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute long-standing customer's second cursed enchanted sword -- premium 160 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7 }] },\n     