and `insuranceValue` in one place.\n   - Simplifies `validateItemTypes` to check a single source of truth.\n   - Improves Rule 3 (No Duplication) and Rule 4 (Fewest Elements).\n\n2. **Simplified `processClaim` payout calculation**  \n   - Replaced `cappedPayout` and `roundedPayout` intermediates with a single `payout` binding.\n   - Keeps the intent clear while reducing elements.\n\n## Rule Evaluation\n\n- **Rule 1 — Tests Pass:** ✅ All 35 tests still pass.\n- **Rule 2 — Reveals Intent:** Names remain descriptive; combined record makes the pairing of base premium and insurance value explicit.\n- **Rule 3 — No Duplication:** Item-type keys are no longer duplicated across two records.\n- **Rule 4 — Fewest Elements:** Removed one intermediate variable and one redundant record.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\n✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (35 tests) 6ms\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  35 passed (35)\n```\n\nRefactoring complete."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 35\nRecent changes: Added validation to reject negative damage amounts\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 35\nRecent changes: Added validation to reject negative damage amounts\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784921103298},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to refactor the implementation in src/claim-office.ts while keeping all tests green. I need to follow the refactoring rules carefully. Let me start by reading the test file and implementation file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the test file and implementation to evaluate the code."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":78,"output":94,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":42,"totalTokens":5740,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784921103318,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-41c16981-81b9-4863-997f-9fc915480a51","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Base premiums and empty input\n  it(\"should return only the processing fee for an empty item list -- premium 5 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single sword -- final premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single amulet -- final premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single staff -- final premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 93 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single potion -- final premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 49 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should calculate premium for a single rune component -- final premium 33 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Component building blocks\n  it(\"should charge per component for 2 runes -- final premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply block discount for exactly 3 alike runes -- final premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should not apply block discount for 4 runes -- final premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should charge per component for 7 runes -- final premium 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Alike components\n  it(\"should not group different component types into a block -- final premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 88 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should create two separate blocks for 3 runes and 3 moonstones -- final premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n        { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 137 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Item-specific modifiers\n  it(\"should add curse surcharge for a cursed sword -- final premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should add high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 5 -- final premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should stack curse and high-enchantment surcharges -- final premium 195 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 195 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Policy-wide modifiers\n  it(\"should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years -- final premium 95 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 95 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply first-insurance surcharge on the first quote -- final premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on second quote -- final premiums 115 G and 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }, { premium: 100 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Multi-item and integration\n  it(\"should apply item-specific modifiers only to affected items in a multi-item policy -- final premium 231 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n        { type: \"sword\", cursed: true },\n        { type: \"amulet\" },\n      ] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 231 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute newcomer with cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should compute long-standing customer's second cursed enchanted sword -- premium 160 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [] },\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7 }] },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }, { premium: 160 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Rounding\n  it(\"should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor -- 197.5 G -> 198 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor -- 350.5 G -> 350 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 8 }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 901 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 350, remainingCap: 1650 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Claim processing - basic reimbursement\n  it(\"should reimburse a regular steel sword damage minus deductible -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should reimburse a rune damage minus deductible -- payout 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }, { payout: 100, remainingCap: 400 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Claim processing - special clauses\n  it(\"should apply 50% reimbursement for enchantment >= 8 then deductible -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 8 }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage then deductible -- payout 700 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5 }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 700, remainingCap: 1300 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should let high-enchantment 50% rule override dragon material -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9 }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }, { payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Claim processing - multiple damages and caps\n  it(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in a single incident -- payout 600 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [\n          { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 },\n          { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2 },\n        ] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon attack\", damages: [\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n          { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 },\n        ] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 181 }, { payout: 600, remainingCap: 2600 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should treat each damage entry as separate event with its own deductible -- payout 800 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"dragon attack\", damages: [\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n          { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n        ] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 225 }, { payout: 800, remainingCap: 3200 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum across multiple claims -- payouts 1400 G and 600 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] } },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"flood\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [\n      { premium: 115 },\n      { payout: 1400, remainingCap: 600 },\n      { payout: 600, remainingCap: 0 },\n    ] });\n  });\n  it(\"should base cap on unmodified insurance value ignoring premium modifiers -- cap 2000 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] } },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }, { payout: 900, remainingCap: 1100 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Error handling\n  it(\"should reject a quote with an unknown item type\", () => {\n    expect(() =>\n      processScenario({\n        customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"broomstick\" }] }],\n      }),\n    ).toThrow(\"Unknown item type: broomstick\");\n  });\n  it(\"should reject a claim for an item not in the policy\", () => {\n    expect(() =>\n      processScenario({\n        customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        steps: [\n          { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n          { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 200 }] } },\n        ],\n      }),\n    ).toThrow(\"Item type amulet is not part of the policy\");\n  });\n  it(\"should reject a claim with negative damage amount\", () => {\n    expect(() =>\n      processScenario({\n        customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        steps: [\n          { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n          { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: -200 }] } },\n        ],\n      }),\n    ).toThrow(\"Damage amount cannot be negative\");\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784921104141},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const rateBasedAdjustment = (\n  applies: boolean,\n  base: number,\n  rate: number,\n): number => (applies ? base * rate : 0);\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst LOYALTY_RATE = 0.2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst CURSE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.3;\n\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\ntype Item = { type: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number; material?: string };\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items?: Item[] };\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: { cause: string; damages: Damage[] } };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ntype Scenario = {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (itemType: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[itemType] ?? 0;\nconst insuranceValueFor = (itemType: string): number => INSURANCE_VALUES[itemType] ?? 0;\n\nconst validateItemTypes = (items: Item[]): void => {\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (!(item.type in BASE_PREMIUMS) || !(item.type in INSURANCE_VALUES)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst countItemsByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst premiumForComponentGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES.includes(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PRICE;\n  }\n  return count * basePremiumFor(type);\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItems = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of countItemsByType(items)) {\n    total += premiumForComponentGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst itemSurchargeAmount = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumFor(item.type);\n  const curseSurcharge = rateBasedAdjustment(item.cursed ?? false, base, CURSE_RATE);\n  const enchantmentSurcharge = rateBasedAdjustment(\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n    base,\n    HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE,\n  );\n  return curseSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst quotePremium = (\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  isFollowUp: boolean,\n): number => {\n  const itemsBase = basePremiumForItems(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + itemSurchargeAmount(item), 0);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = itemsBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount = rateBasedAdjustment(\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD,\n    itemsBase,\n    LOYALTY_RATE,\n  );\n  const followUpDiscount = rateBasedAdjustment(\n    isFollowUp,\n    itemsBase,\n    FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_RATE,\n  );\n  const subtotal =\n    itemsBase +\n    itemSurcharges +\n    firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n    loyaltyDiscount -\n    followUpDiscount +\n    PROCESSING_FEE;\n  return Math.ceil(subtotal);\n};\n\ntype Policy = { items: Item[]; cap: number };\n\nconst policyInsuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueFor(item.type), 0);\n\nconst policyCapFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  policyInsuranceSum(items) * POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst damageReimbursementRate = (item: Item): number =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD ? DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE : 1;\n\nconst damagePayout = (damage: Damage, item: Item): number => {\n  const reimbursement = damage.amount * damageReimbursementRate(item);\n  return Math.max(0, reimbursement - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst validateDamages = (damages: Damage[]): void => {\n  for (const damage of damages) {\n    if (damage.amount < 0) {\n      throw new Error(\"Damage amount cannot be negative\");\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: ClaimStep[\"incident\"]): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  validateDamages(incident.damages);\n  const rawPayout = incident.damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (!item) {\n      throw new Error(`Item type ${damage.itemType} is not part of the policy`);\n    }\n    return sum + damagePayout(damage, item);\n  }, 0);\n  const cappedPayout = Math.min(rawPayout, policy.cap);\n  const roundedPayout = Math.floor(cappedPayout);\n  return { payout: roundedPayout, remainingCap: policy.cap - roundedPayout };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): { results: Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> } => {\n  const results: Array<{ premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number }> = [];\n  const policies: Policy[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      validateItemTypes(items);\n      const isFollowUp = policies.length > 0;\n      policies.push({ items, cap: policyCapFor(items) });\n      results.push({ premium: quotePremium(items, scenario.customer, isFollowUp) });\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policy = policies[step.policy];\n      const result = processClaim(policy, step.incident);\n      policy.cap = result.remainingCap;\n      results.push(result);\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784921104141},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have both files. Let me run the tests first to confirm they all pass, then analyze the code for refactoring opportunities.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":5688,"output":51,"cacheRead":5696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":27,"totalTokens":11435,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784921104142,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-a648d1e3-2911-4ebb-aeb9-6e0aceebc5f8","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-59-44_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (35 tests) 12ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  35 passed (35)\n   Start at  19:25:05\n   Duration  178ms (transform 37ms, setup 0ms, collect 36ms, tests 12ms, environment 0ms, prepare 45ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784921105592},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 35 tests pass. Now I need to evaluate naming first, then calculate APP mass, then apply simple design rules.\n\nLet me analyze the code:\n\n**Naming Evaluation:**\n- `processScenario` - This is the main export. It processes a scenario with quotes and claims. Name seems reasonable.\n- `rateBasedAdjustment` - applies a rate-based adjustment if condition is true. Could be clearer, but it's okay.\n- `basePremiumFor` - gets base premium for item type. Good.\n- `insuranceValueFor` - gets insurance value for item type. Good.\n- `validateItemTypes` - validates item types. Good.\n- `countItemsByType` - counts items by type. Good.\n- `premiumForComponentGroup` - calculates premium for a group of components. Good.\n- `basePremiumForItems` - calculates base premium for items. Good.\n- `itemSurchargeAmount` - calculates surcharge amount for an item. Good.\n- `quotePremium` - calculates quote premium. Good.\n- `policyInsuranceSum` - calculates insurance sum for policy. Good.\n- `policyCapFor` - calculates policy cap. Good.\n- `damageReimbursementRate` - gets reimbursement rate for damage. Good.\n- `damagePayout` - calculates damage payout. Good.\n- `validateDamages` - validates damages. Good.\n- `processClaim` - processes a claim. Good.\n\nPotential naming issues:\n1. `rateBasedAdjustment` - It conditionally applies a rate adjustment. Maybe `applyRateIf` or `conditionalRateAdjustment`? But the current name is fine.\n\n**APP Mass Calculation:**\n\nLet me count components in the implementation file. I'll count each function separately and sum.\n\nConstants: PROCESSING_FEE, COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE, COMPONENT_BLOCK_PRICE, FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE, LOYALTY_THRESHOLD, LOYALTY_RATE, FOLLOW_UP_CONTRACT_RATE, CURSE_RATE, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE, DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE, DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD, DAMAGE_ENCHANTMENT_RATE, POLICY_CAP_MULTIPLIER = 14\nBASE_PREMIUMS object literals: sword:100, amulet:60, staff:80, potion:40, rune:25, moonstone:25 = 6\nINSURANCE_VALUES object literals: sword:1000, amulet:600, staff:800, potion:400, rune:250, moonstone:250 = 6\nCOMPONENT_BLOCK_TYPES array: \"rune\", \"moonstone\" = 2 literals\nTotal constants: 14 + 6 + 6 + 2 = 28\n\nBindings: \n- rateBasedAdjustment: applies, base, rate = 3\n- basePremiumFor: itemTyp